WEBVTT

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.670
We barged into the family lodge
those rogue samurai ran into,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.110
but the head clerk stopped us!

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.070
He stopped you?

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:14.860
Yeah.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.810
He kept goin’, “Who
ordered you to do this?

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.870
Go get the local police.”

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.750
And that’s how you lost those ronin?

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.250
Dammit!

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:29.520
What’re the people of Kyoto thinking
defendin’ those rogue samurai?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:35.460
We lack any real track record and
the imperial nationalist party,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.270
especially the Choshu ronin,
are said to grease people’s fingers.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.470
For having just drawn someone’s blood,

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.890
you seem rather calm, Hajime-kun.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.550
Saito, having crossed blades with them,
what do you think?

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.690
They were all lacking
in skill with the sword.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:05.790
But due to our limited numbers,

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.380
I am concerned when I
consider what would happen

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.540
should the enemy surround us.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.320
But it would take time

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:15.980
and money to enlist new
recruits and train them.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.770
For now, never go out alone.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.840
Getting yourself killed
won’t do us any good.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:26.020
At any rate, there just isn’t
enough stuff we can do.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:31.070
Say, what happened to workin’
for the Aizu Domain?

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.270
We shall be sending an official
petition to Lord Aizu

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.590
for permission to remain
in Kyoto shortly.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.030
Any chance they’ll give
us permission to stay?

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.100
I cannot say.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.390
Depending on their answer, there is a

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.590
possibility that we will
have to leave Kyoto.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.590
Truly, our fate rests on Serizawa-san’s
connections and course of action.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:59.880
Just tell yourself that we are using him.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.330
I can’t make myself that
emotionally detached from this!

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:06.100
You can call say that’s
what makes me green,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.560
but I swear that someday
I will outwit that man

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.730
and elevate Kondou-san to
a higher place of power!

00:03:55.710 --> 00:04:00.710
EPISODE 3:
Rules for a Pack of Wolves

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:04.970
Everyone, listen up!

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:09.500
We just received a letter from Lord Aizu,

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:10.980
the Kyoto Military Commissioner.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.750
He is going to officially
place us under his charge.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.520
Sweet!

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:21.020
Now we can go all-out with our patrols!

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.690
Man, this is great!

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.990
It looks like we’re gonna
to be gettin’ busy.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.030
My, isn’t this wonderful news?

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.900
Yeah, it’s great that Lord
Aizu acknowledged our ability!

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.970
It’s amazing how Serizawa-sensei
swayed the Shogunate!

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.500
Isn’t it, Tonouchi-kun?

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.970
Indeed!

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.470
You’re over-reacting.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:41.510
Not at all! Remember what they said?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.640
He said he was willing to grant us
permission to remain in Kyoto

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.610
with you standing at the
center of our corps!

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.860
The results would have been

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:51.330
different without you, Serizawa-dono!

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:56.590
Well then, let’s drink to
our success at Shimabara.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.560
Nagakura-kun, come join us.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:02.150
Eh?

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:06.370
N-nah, it would hurt your name if a

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.910
good-fer-nothin’ like me were seen with you.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.780
My name is not so fragile that you

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.910
could damage it by acting somewhat rowdy.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.900
In-in that case, uh...
Heisuke and Sano’re comin'!

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.610
The more the merrier and all!

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.420
Souji, Saito, you’re
comin’ too, right? Right?

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.820
Kondou-kun, naturally you
will come join me as well.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.760
Well... This is a bit embarrassing,
but I abstain from alcohol.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.460
What, you can’t drink?

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.690
Isn’t that bad for a warrior
who speaks of politics?

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.540
Please go out and enjoy yourselves.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.070
What about you?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:50.010
I bet you haven’t been to a
red-light district, have you, Feral Dog?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:51.950
There’s no way--

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.450
Ryunosuke said he’s coming!

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.570
Go on! Feel free to drink
as much as you want!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.710
Um, it would seem you are not
indulging in your drinks.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.320
Yeah, I can’t drink SAKE.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.490
They just forced me to tag along.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.550
Hey, Okita!

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.710
You’ve got an odd sense
of taste to stare at

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.010
us men after coming to
the red-light district.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.880
Not really.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.060
I’m not all that interested
in places like this.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:56.520
Hmmm. Then what are you doing here?

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.510
Isn’t it obvious?

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:00.140
I thought I might catch

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.020
a good opportunity
to cut you down if I came with you.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:08.190
Cut me down?

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.620
A snot-nosed brat like you?

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:13.760
What a great joke!

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.670
Your death threats mean nothing to me.

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:26.300
Although I cannot say the
same for that Hijikata guy.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.550
Hijikata-san?

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:32.510
When that man glared at
me at the Honjou Inn,

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:36.560
even I felt chills there for a second!

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.760
Compared to him,

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:42.060
your threats to kill
me sound like a childish prater.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.620
If you like, I’d be willing
to truly kill you...

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:47.570
Souji.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:52.570
He’s killed more than
just one or two men.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:59.470
He is far more imposing than you.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.160
Please allow her to join you.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.970
I am Kosuzu.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:36.740
Bitch!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.080
Do you know who you are talking to?!

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:43.870
How dare a lowly MAIKO speak
to me in such a manner?!

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:47.880
I merely said precisely what I thought!

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.630
Do you know who I am?!

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.660
You are a powerful samurai, are you not?

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:57.040
Then please do not take advantage of your

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:00.190
money and rank to act
with such arrogance!

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.640
Say what?!

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:04.070
Serizawa-han, please forgive her!

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:05.880
She is still but a child.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.320
Kosuzu-chan, hurry and apologize!

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.610
No. There is nothing
wrong with what I said.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.670
What are you doing, Serizawa-san?!

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:20.530
Cut it out!

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.370
You’re in my way!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:29.110
Now, now! C’mon, Serizawa-san!

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.190
This is supposed to be a party.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:33.350
Please let it slide.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:36.300
Lookie! We’ve still
got some awesome SAKE!

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.040
You should go.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.530
Leave the rest to us.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.040
I appreciate it.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.080
Come, Kosuzu-chan! Hurry!

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:45.710
Okay.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:49.020
I’ll go get Hijikata-san.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:49.900
Yeah.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.570
Careful. Watch your step.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.320
I am terribly sorry.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.160
I did not mean to inconvenience you...

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.570
Hey, you okay?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.930
By protecting me, you got...

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:06.630
Please forgive me.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:07.730
F-forget it.

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:09.960
He’s always like that.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:12.960
I’m sorry we put you through that.

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:15.010
You’re bleeding!

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:17.970
I’m fine. This is nothing.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:24.970
Anyway, you’re nuts to defy a
warrior when you’re just a girl!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.820
Shouldn’t a MAIKO simply keep
quiet and pour the SAKE?

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.860
We are not toys!

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.610
We have hearts that can feel
frustration and sadness!

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.110
They try to use force to
suppress those feelings!

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.610
I loathe all samurai!

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.130
Hey! What’s that for?!

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.650
You were pretty cool back there.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:59.050
Although you blew it there at the end.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:04.510
Serizawa-san, what the
hell happened here?!

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:09.330
I merely chastised her
for her rude behavior.

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:13.520
It wouldn’t have gotten this
carried away if that’s all you did!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:18.040
Sensei, let’s leave this
to Kondou-kun and move on.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:27.910
He does whatever he wants!

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:31.820
We are no different than
those rogue samurai!

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.730
Considering all the
commotion he stirred...

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:42.800
We’ll have to bind him
with a set of rules.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.180
He’ll commit honorable
suicide if he breaks them.

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:46.330
Honorable suicide?!

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:52.240
What on earth are you doing here?

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:56.240
Well, I just so happened
to be passing by.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:59.030
I-I wasn’t eavesdropping or anything!

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.280
Sorry for disturbing you.

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:04.030
A moment please, Ibuki-kun.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.250
How have things been going of late?

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:12.920
Has Serizawa-san been
treating you poorly?

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:16.100
Well, yeah, but that’s nothing new.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.920
What brought this on?

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:22.000
Ibuki-kun, if you like,

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.320
why don’t you join the Roshigumi
as an official soldier?

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:29.710
Eh?! But I can’t use
a sword worth diddly!

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:32.590
You would simply need to
start training henceforth.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:34.400
We even offer a salary.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.900
Yeah, but...

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:39.920
Don’t push any further, Sannan-san.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:43.200
Someone like him would just trip us up.

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:44.700
Excuse me?!

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.320
We don’t need the likes
of you in the Roshigumi!

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.200
Now get your butt out of here.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:55.560
It’s not like I’m here
because I want to be!

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:58.510
I have absolutely no intention of
becoming a samurai to begin with!

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.480
Goodness gracious.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:07.000
And here we could use as
many allies as we could get.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.050
Don’t play dumb, Sannan-san.

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.190
There is no way you would recruit

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.850
someone who can’t use a sword.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.870
You were essentially
scheming to rope him in

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.150
so you could wring out information

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.990
regarding Serizawa-san, weren’t you?

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.480
So you saw through my plan?

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.030
I’ve known you for a long time.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:28.320
Is it safe to assume you do not
want to drag him into this?

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:33.500
Hijikata-kun, you are far too kind.

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:36.440
There is something I would like

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:40.040
to go over with you regarding our future.

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:43.670
We would like to structure ourselves
as a proper organization.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.760
Please look this over.

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:53.400
The chiefs would be composed
of Serizawa-sensei

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:55.740
and I as well as Kondou-kun, huh?

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:59.750
Hijikata-kun and Sannan-kun
would be the commanders and...

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:03.780
And here are the rules of conduct
to keep the men in line.

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:08.240
One: Do not deviate from
the Way of the Warrior.

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.380
Two: Desertion will not be tolerated.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:15.010
Three: Do not raise money
without authorization.

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:18.290
Four: Do not manage another’s
litigation without authorization.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:21.790
Five: Personal duels
will not be tolerated.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:24.480
Whosoever breaks any of the rules listed

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.800
to the right must commit
honorable suicide.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.330
Wh-what is with these rules?!

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.200
The soldiers who rally
under us in the future

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:36.240
will hail from various
ranks and walks of life.

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:39.240
The only way to keep the crowd in check

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.540
is to clamp down on
them with strict rules.

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.580
“Rules of Conduct,” eh?

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.650
I’m amazed you were able to come
up with something like this.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.620
But with such a strict code...

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:52.660
Say something, Serizawa-sensei!

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:55.960
Violators must commit honorable suicide.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:57.080
Isn’t that right?

00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:00.580
Yeah, even if you’re
a chief or commander.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.090
I see...

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:09.340
Serizawa-san appeared
rather calm, didn’t he?

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:13.340
Regardless of what he
thinks, rules are rules.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:15.560
He simply has to obey them.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:20.760
Serizawa-sensei, is it wise
to let them do as they wish?

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.220
Even with that code,

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:30.590
their hands are tied if they lack
the power to see it obeyed.

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:34.070
Yeah... You have a point, but...

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:40.250
Dang, those rules are stupid!

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.600
What the hell were they thinking?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.130
Those rules of conduct were
definitely too strict.

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:49.200
If Kondou-san feels those
rules are necessary,

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.130
I will obey them.

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:53.250
That goes for me, too...

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:58.020
But I don’t like my friends getting
tied down by those rules...

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:01.350
We will probably need
it for the new recruits

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.370
we will be getting henceforth.

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:05.960
I know that!

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:09.020
But it’s kinda different
from what I had imagined...

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.630
If I had taken him up on
that offer back there...

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:15.910
Why don’t you join the Roshigumi?

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.140
You should probably be careful yourself.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.110
It’s not like I’m a
member of the Roshigumi!

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:27.420
But if Serizawa-san had
to slice open his gut,

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:30.920
I bet you’d have to follow suit...

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:36.180
I’m leaving before I get
caught up in any of this crap!

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:45.560
Pile it on!

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.000
You got it.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.440
The fragrance of this house is superb.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:54.170
When eating freshly cooked
white rice while enjoying the aroma,

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:57.200
its true value becomes evident.

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:00.610
Nothing is more complex than
the simple things in life.

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:03.450
Huh...

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:08.250
Shinpatsu, what do you
think you’re doing?!

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:11.320
See, in our world the
strong eat the weak.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:13.430
In that case, I’ll--!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.800
Why, you! You--! You--!

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.300
Ryunosuke, don’t let your guard down!

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:22.670
You better be careful!

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:24.340
Take someone’s food
before they take yours!

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:26.740
Really?

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.360
Then I won’t hold back.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:34.610
If you need me for something,
wait until after I’m done eating.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:38.050
In the world of beasts, you
have no right to complain

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:40.390
if you get killed by disturbing
a stronger animal’s meal.

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:44.720
Furthermore, this is one
of my favorite dishes.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:46.760
Never go after it!

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:52.250
G-got it! M-my bad!

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:58.760
You must not value your life.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:02.640
Of all the people here, I can’t believe
you went after Saito’s food.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.740
I’m the type that eats
his favorite food first!

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:09.580
Sorry for the wait!

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:10.820
I’ve been waitin’ for this!

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:13.840
What is this pickle? Weeds?

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:15.220
Are they even edible?

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:17.660
That’s called mibuna.

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:22.300
Farmers put their blood
and sweat into growing it,

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.730
so don’t be a picky eater.

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:25.500
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:29.000
Kondou-san is so stern about stuff like

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.040
that since he used to be a farmer.

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:33.550
He wasn’t born into the warrior class?

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:37.550
Nope, but he’s crazy strong when
he picks up a wooden sword.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:41.550
Shuusai Kondou-sensei of the Shieikan
saw promise in him

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.560
and adopted him to be his heir.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:52.740
Toshi, why don’t you put work out of
your mind while you’re eating?

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:55.900
Yeah, I should...

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:01.700
What are you doing, Kondou-san?!

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:02.980
That wasn’t enough, was it?

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.270
Eat up.

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:07.330
But you still haven’t eaten a bite!

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:09.610
Back in our Shieikan days,

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:12.540
you frequently shared your food with me.

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:14.980
What brought this on?

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:16.240
Knock it off!

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:20.720
We’re beyond such
formalities, aren’t we?

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.090
You’re absolutely right!

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:29.350
Jeez, you’re unbelievable...

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:33.110
No matter what the situation,
you always place others before yourself.

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:34.800
Do you remember that one time, Toshi?

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:38.110
I was out and someone
came to crush our dojo.

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:42.650
Anyway, we’re finally in the
service of the Aizu Domain!

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.860
Couldn’t we afford
to upgrade our dinner?

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:47.120
Well, Hijikata-san?

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:52.120
That will have to wait
until they start paying us.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:03.460
Well, they are probably
uncertain as to whether or not

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.250
we are worthy of their trust.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:07.330
Is that right...?

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:12.890
Thank you for the meal.

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:15.640
Souji, that was fast.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:17.780
I need to get in some sword practice.

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:20.860
Right now, every second counts.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:25.910
Practicing right after you
eat is bad for your body.

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:29.620
Shinpachi-san and
Hajime-kun got it lucky.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:33.420
I’m dying to slay a bunch
of those rogue samurai.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.920
What a thing to say.

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:42.420
Souji, haven’t you been
acting strange lately?

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:47.810
Souji, I want you to go back to Edo.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:53.310
That joke isn’t the least bit funny.

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:58.350
Lately Serizawa-san’s influence
is making you go on about

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:00.340
how you want to cut down or kill people.

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:02.790
You’re still a kid.

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:04.920
He’s making you lose sight of yourself.

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:08.960
Hijikata-san, you just
think I’m in the way

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:10.830
because I stick by
Kondou-san, don’t you?!

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:14.580
If that’s what you’d like
to think, then go ahead.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:18.970
Toshi, why did you
suddenly bring this up?

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:23.180
We’re in Kyoto to defend the peace.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:26.170
But he wants to kill.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:28.070
That’s all he’s thinking about.

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:31.850
We can’t let someone
like that stay here!

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:35.690
Souji--

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:38.590
No! There is no way I’m going back!

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:42.930
I’m going to stay here
and help you, Kondou-san!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:45.040
Souji!

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:51.990
Damn it!

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:33.890
I will help you even more, Kondou-san.

00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:38.640
I did not want him to soil his
name by killing a comrade!

00:23:39.090 --> 00:23:41.400
Souji, whose blood is that...?

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:43.400
NEXT EPISODE:
The Blade Drenched in Blood
